WEBVTT

NOTE v3 English captions for Mountain Pose. Soft Jenny voice, phonetic Sanskrit.

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.450
This is Mountain Pose.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.206
In Sanskrit it is called tah dah sah nah.

3
00:00:09.006 --> 00:00:13.686
Once more, slowly: tah dah sah nah.

4
00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:18.294
Here is what this pose is for.

5
00:00:18.994 --> 00:00:22.642
It can help you improve your posture.

6
00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:27.800
It gently builds strength in the legs and the core.

7
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.678
It is a simple way to practice balance and body awareness.

8
00:00:34.228 --> 00:00:37.924
And it can help the mind feel calm.

9
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:46.864
Please be careful if standing still is uncomfortable. You can stand near a wall.

10
00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:52.548
Let's do it together, one step at a time.

11
00:00:53.548 --> 00:01:00.964
Step one. Stand at the top of your mat, and bring your feet together.

12
00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:07.400
You may also keep them a little apart, if that feels more steady.

13
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.996
Step two. Press down through all four corners of each foot.

14
00:01:15.646 --> 00:01:20.950
Lift your toes, spread them, and set them down again.

15
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:31.306
Step three. Gently firm your thighs, and keep a soft bend in the knees if your legs want to lock.

16
00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:38.174
Roll your shoulders back and down, and turn your palms to face forward.

17
00:01:39.074 --> 00:01:50.066
Step four. Reach the top of your head up. Soften your face, and look at one still point in front of you.

18
00:01:51.066 --> 00:01:56.610
Breathe in, and out, through your nose, slow and even.

19
00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.322
Just stay, and breathe.

20
00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:09.626
A common mistake: do not lock your knees, and do not lean back on your heels.

21
00:02:10.326 --> 00:02:14.046
Keep your weight in the middle of your feet.

22
00:02:15.046 --> 00:02:20.206
An easier version: stand with your back near a wall.

23
00:02:20.856 --> 00:02:29.400
Let your heels sit a few inches away, and lightly touch the wall with your shoulder blades and the back of your head.

24
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:37.984
Hold for about thirty to sixty seconds, then relax your arms and soften your knees.
